WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.377 --> 00:00:18.964
- [Narrator] The Honest Company Steps Up.

00:00:18.964 --> 00:00:21.164
Everyone I approached was skeptical.

00:00:21.164 --> 00:00:25.199
Even my husband, Cash,
thought the idea was too big.

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:29.185
Jessica Alba, co-founder
of The Honest Company.

00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:32.122
The Honest Company took it's
one word to the next level.

00:00:32.122 --> 00:00:34.248
Not only did co-founders Jessica Alba

00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:37.225
and Christopher Gavigan embrace
the one word philosophy,

00:00:37.225 --> 00:00:42.081
they named their business
after their one word, honest.

00:00:42.081 --> 00:00:44.668
Jessica and Christopher were
disgusted by how unhealthy

00:00:44.668 --> 00:00:46.819
many children's products are.

00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:48.210
They are laced with toxic chemicals

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.246
that haven't been properly tested.

00:00:50.246 --> 00:00:53.372
They were making kids and Jessica sick.

00:00:53.372 --> 00:00:56.370
She and Christopher got fed up.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.947
So they decided to be the change

00:00:57.947 --> 00:00:59.979
they wanted to see in the world.

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:02.482
They launched The Honest
Company to provide non-toxic,

00:01:02.482 --> 00:01:06.060
eco-friendly, fashionable, and
affordable products for kids

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.463
ranging from diapers to
bath and body products.

00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:11.541
They believed in their business
so much that they hired

00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:14.142
Jessica's mom to work for them.

00:01:14.142 --> 00:01:16.448
They loved their manifestoian
product so deeply,

00:01:16.448 --> 00:01:18.920
that they hang them on their wall.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.189
Jessica practices honest
management and the actress

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:23.779
entrepreneur worth over
200 million dollars,

00:01:23.779 --> 00:01:26.283
doesn't have her own office.

00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:29.139
She sits right along side her team.

00:01:29.139 --> 00:01:31.094
They don't test their products on animals.

00:01:31.094 --> 00:01:33.563
They test them on their own children.

00:01:33.563 --> 00:01:34.976
They give one percent of their revenue

00:01:34.976 --> 00:01:37.243
to charity in chemical research.

00:01:37.243 --> 00:01:39.092
From their employees, to their suppliers,

00:01:39.092 --> 00:01:41.929
they think about the impact
they're leaving on the world.

00:01:41.929 --> 00:01:43.502
To reduce their carbon footprint,

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:45.642
everything they make is
produced within 150 miles

00:01:45.642 --> 00:01:49.392
of Los Angeles and they
ship ground, not air.

00:01:50.698 --> 00:01:53.122
They have unapologetically
high standards in products,

00:01:53.122 --> 00:01:55.018
people, and business practices.

00:01:55.018 --> 00:01:56.009
Everything they do

00:01:56.009 --> 00:01:58.886
has to match up with
their honest philosophy.

00:01:58.886 --> 00:02:00.092
The results?

00:02:00.092 --> 00:02:02.348
The Honest Company went from zero to

00:02:02.348 --> 00:02:05.207
hundreds of millions of dollars in sales.

00:02:05.207 --> 00:02:06.431
After three years in business,

00:02:06.431 --> 00:02:09.258
the company was valued
at one billion dollars.

00:02:09.258 --> 00:02:10.770
They are making money and making

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.690
an impact by following their one word.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.345
So I asked Christopher to
share his one word story.

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:19.393
- [Christopher] Early in my
career, I was frustrated.

00:02:19.393 --> 00:02:20.609
I was frustrated with the lack of

00:02:20.609 --> 00:02:23.156
authentic relationships in business.

00:02:23.156 --> 00:02:25.228
I was frustrated when I
saw that everyone would

00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:26.597
promise you the world

00:02:26.597 --> 00:02:29.246
and then there was no
consistent follow-up.

00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:31.716
That's being totally dishonest.

00:02:31.716 --> 00:02:34.594
What I found was the levels of
transparency and authenticity

00:02:34.594 --> 00:02:37.680
and clarity and willingness
to tell the consumer what was

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.720
healthy and safe weren't there.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.769
And I'm thinking, wow, these
are products that we are using

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:46.706
on our bodies, in our
homes, on our children.

00:02:46.706 --> 00:02:48.086
We're ingesting them.

00:02:48.086 --> 00:02:50.626
How is that possible?

00:02:50.626 --> 00:02:51.970
When my business partner Jessica and I

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.241
were developing our concept,
we were imagining the world.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.587
Dreaming big and what we wanted in it.

00:02:57.587 --> 00:03:00.365
We were thinking about
what's the world we wanted?

00:03:00.365 --> 00:03:03.085
I love the beauty of the word, honest.

00:03:03.085 --> 00:03:04.457
The simplicity.

00:03:04.457 --> 00:03:07.299
To be honest is something
that everyone wants to be.

00:03:07.299 --> 00:03:10.489
It's an aspiration as well
as a real life fulfillment.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.731
It's an honor to hold that word.

00:03:12.731 --> 00:03:14.881
It's a privilege and it's a duty.

00:03:14.881 --> 00:03:16.181
It holds you to a standard

00:03:16.181 --> 00:03:20.038
and it drives us forward every single day.

00:03:20.038 --> 00:03:22.040
I wanted to challenge ourselves.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.094
To be honest.

00:03:23.094 --> 00:03:24.183
What does that mean?

00:03:24.183 --> 00:03:25.451
That's a lot to live up to.

00:03:25.451 --> 00:03:28.210
I wanted to see if we could do it.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.586
We're constantly, as a
brand and as a company,

00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:34.272
pushing ourselves to really
achieve, to be more and more

00:03:34.272 --> 00:03:36.272
honest every single day.

00:03:37.188 --> 00:03:39.575
Everyone is here to see this
mission and purpose-driven

00:03:39.575 --> 00:03:41.574
company fulfill its core goal

00:03:41.574 --> 00:03:45.018
and a lot of it is we're
not here to build product.

00:03:45.018 --> 00:03:45.957
We're here to educate

00:03:45.957 --> 00:03:48.722
a new generation of consumers and parents.

00:03:48.722 --> 00:03:51.316
In our core mission, we
don't talk about product.

00:03:51.316 --> 00:03:55.063
We talk about what's the change
in the world we want to see

00:03:55.063 --> 00:03:57.503
and how do we accomplish that?

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.441
You have to align yourself
with what you believe is right.

00:04:00.441 --> 00:04:03.119
What I love about us is we
really act from our heart

00:04:03.119 --> 00:04:07.023
and if it doesn't feel right,
we're not going to go there.

00:04:07.023 --> 00:04:08.518
Honesty is telling people the truth

00:04:08.518 --> 00:04:11.100
even though it might be uncomfortable.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.161
It's quality.

00:04:12.161 --> 00:04:13.763
It's saying what matters.

00:04:13.763 --> 00:04:15.349
It's telling people what you won't do

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:18.817
and what's not inside as
opposed to what is inside.

00:04:18.817 --> 00:04:21.019
We're everything from a
baby diaper to shampoo

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:24.911
to fruit and veggie washes to
a range of lifestyle products.

00:04:24.911 --> 00:04:28.431
At the end of the day, a
parent just wants to trust you.

00:04:28.431 --> 00:04:30.075
I guard that trust.

00:04:30.075 --> 00:04:32.483
I safeguard it every single day.

00:04:32.483 --> 00:04:34.065
It's the only thing we have.

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:35.930
Our credibility and trust.

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.104
I am such a strong, passionate advocate

00:04:38.104 --> 00:04:40.567
of keeping that trust and
that level of connectivity

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.634
with the consumer and letting them know

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:46.002
we are doing everything
possible every single day

00:04:46.002 --> 00:04:48.454
to build and improve
on that level of trust

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.704
and connected relationship.

